cards.back:
The `*` operator, when used with a pointer variable, accesses the value stored at the memory address that the pointer holds. It "dereferences" the pointer to get to the actual data.
```c
int value = 100;
int *p_value = &value;
printf("%d", *p_value); // Output: 100 (accesses the value of 'value')
```

